63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Looking at these, Candidate A seems wonderful. It uses local craftspeople for demonstrations, which satisfies the visitors' desire for human interaction without overtaxing our tired conservation staff or requiring expensive, fragile machinery.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, I agree. Candidate A minimizes the risk of shipping delays and high transport costs since it is local. It is the most logical choice to avoid the logistical failures we've seen in past seasons.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,May,,"Candidate A is great, but look at Candidate B! A working conservation bench is exactly the kind of ""people working"" vibe visitors love, and it's municipal, so it's local and low-risk for shipping.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@May, Candidate B is risky. A working conservation bench might be too heavy for the suspended bay, and the lab is already severely backlogged. Candidate A is much safer for the building and the staff.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Sakura,,@Misaki is right! Candidate B sounds like it needs a lot of heavy stuff and more work for the tired lab people. Candidate A is way better because it's local and simple! I vote for A!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, while Candidate B is tempting, we must remember the conservation lab is struggling. Adding a public bench might put too much pressure on our one remaining staff member. Candidate A is much kinder to our team.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@May, Candidate C is a logistical nightmare given the maintenance logs and rigging risks, and Candidate D relies too heavily on loans. Candidate A is the only one that aligns with all our constraints. I vote for A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shion, you're right about C and D. I still love the idea of B, but if the lab is that stressed, it's not fair to the staff. A gives us those live demos visitors crave. I vote for A!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, I'm glad you agree. Candidate A avoids the weight risks of B and the fragility of C, while remaining easy to secure during evening hires. It is the most sustainable choice. I vote for A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"Everyone is voting for A! It's the winner! It's local, it's friendly, and it won't cost us a mountain of money for fancy mounts or repairs. I'm so happy we found a great one! I vote for A!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shizue,,It is a relief that we have all found a path that respects both our visitors and our hardworking staff. I am very happy to cast my vote for Candidate A.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shion,,"The consensus is absolute. Candidate A is the only proposal that satisfies our logistical, financial, and structural constraints while meeting visitor expectations. I maintain my vote for A.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,May,,I'm completely sold. It's the perfect mix of local charm and the human energy that actually brings people back. I'm happy to go with the group. I vote for A!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Candidate A is the most responsible choice for the gallery's physical health and the staff's wellbeing. I cast my vote for Candidate A.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"Yay! We all agree! It's a total win-win! No money-monsters, no broken floors, and lots of happy people! I'm super-duper happy to vote for Candidate A!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
